go-decimal128-app-benchmark
===========================

Go implementations of the UW-Madison decimal floating-point application
benchmarks, for measuring Go decimal128 libraries.

This repository is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later
(see LICENSE). The GPL obligation comes entirely from the benchmark workloads
described below. The decimal libraries it measures are external Go module
dependencies under their own licenses; they are not copied into this
repository, and this repository does not change their terms.


Attribution and provenance of the benchmark workloads
------------------------------------------------------

* Telco
    Author: Mike Cowlishaw (IBM).
    Source: https://speleotrove.com/decimal/telco.html
            https://speleotrove.com/decimal/telcoSpec.html
    Freely distributable; imposes no GPL obligation. The input data and the
    10-call example under data/telco/ are his published files, from
    https://github.com/migueldecimal128/decimal128-resources (telco/), not the
    UW-Madison suite's modified version. apps/telco/ is MIT: it is based on
    the telco program in decimal128-go (MIT) and is not derived from the
    UW-Madison suite.

* Banking, Tax Preparation, Risk Management, Euro Conversion
    Source: University of Wisconsin-Madison, MESA Lab.
      Decimal Floating-Point (DFP) Benchmark suite, v1.0.
    Papers:
      Liang-Kai Wang, Michael J. Schulte, et al.,
        "Benchmarks and Performance Analysis of Decimal Floating-Point
         Applications," IEEE International Conference on Computer Design
         (ICCD), October 2007.
      Mike Anderson, Charles Tsen, Liang-Kai Wang, Katherine Compton,
        Michael J. Schulte,
        "Performance Analysis of Decimal Floating-Point Libraries and Its
         Impact on Decimal Hardware and Software Solutions," IEEE ICCD,
         October 2009.
    License: GNU General Public License v3.0 (see the suite's source headers,
             e.g. arith.def / operator.h).
    The Tax Preparation benchmark is itself derived from OpenTaxSolver
      (http://opentaxsolver.sourceforge.net/), also GPL-licensed.
    The original suite is included in UW-Madison/: its archive as
      distributed, the C sources, build files, scripts and READMEs extracted
      from it unchanged, and the two papers above (copied from
      https://github.com/migueldecimal128/decimal128-resources, UW-Madison/).

The input data and the euro conversion and banking reference outputs under
data/ are the suite's own files, unchanged and likewise GPLv3. The tax
preparation and risk management reference outputs were regenerated in
decimal128-app-benchmark (see data/README.md).

The Go programs under apps/ are translations of those GPL-licensed C programs,
made in https://github.com/migueldecimal128/decimal128-app-benchmark. They are
DERIVATIVE WORKS and are therefore GPLv3 (per-file header
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later).


